{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-quantum-dilogarithm-volume","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:quantum-dilogarithm-volume","kind":"proposition","title":"Nuclear energy from the quantum dilogarithm of the Markov trace","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-markov-trace-factorization"],"tags":["quantum-dilogarithm","volume","markov-trace","generator-volume","intensive","binding-energy","q-value","topological-mass"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.quantum_dilogarithm_volume","text":"quantum-dilogarithm-volume.md","leanSource":"quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:quantum-dilogarithm-volume\"></a><p>The nuclear binding energy is the quantum dilogarithm volume of the Markov trace, normalized by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q^2</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{E}_{\\mathrm{bind}}(p, n)\n  = \n  \\frac{\\Phi_q(\\mathcal{N}(Z, N))}{\\hbar_q^2},</code></pre>\n<p>where the quantum dilogarithm volume is the logarithm of the Markov trace product:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\Phi_q(\\mathcal{N}(Z, N))\n   := \n  \\sum_{i=0}^{A-2} \\log |z \\cdot a_i + b_i|\n  = \n  \\log \\prod_{i=0}^{A-2} |\\hat{V}_i|.</code></pre>\n<p>This provides the natural <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformation of the hyperbolic volume. At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>, all crossings have equal weight, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{V}_i = 1</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q = 0</code> (no binding). At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code>, the crossing asymmetry generates a nonzero <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q</code>, binding the nucleus.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"16.14.3","page":"b/prop-quantum-dilogarithm-volume","qa":{"counts":{"pass":89,"fail":1,"warn":2,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.quantum_dilogarithm_volume","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/quantum-dilogarithm-volume.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
